			<div class="content" id="post-content-2197258">
									

<p>Who says they know it's blocked? They're sending people through some sort of trans-spatial/temporal/dimensional device. We have no way to know what happens to something that goes in but does not successfully exit. Their bodies may be vaporized or go flying off into some other dimension (for some other Foundation to find and be perplexed by).</p>
<p>Example: Stargate SG-1's stargate has an iris attached to it that is flush with the event horizon of the gate, meaning that anything that hits it is bounced back into the event horizon. Stargates are one way, so anything that tries to go into the receiving gate is destroyed, hence the iris destroys anything or anyone attempting to come through. Anyone still on the sending end has no way of knowing this because nothing comes back through.</p>
<p>So as far as the cat people may know, they are successfully evacuating their friends and family to a safe place and have no clue that they are sending them to their doom.</p>

